 ## JSON Patch
 
+`createPatch(from, to)` creates an [RFC 6902 JSON Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6902)
+that transforms one JSON document into another without changing either input. It emits operations for
+the differing members and array positions, instead of replacing an unchanged document around a small
+change.
+
+```ts
+import { createPatch } from 'json-toolkit';
+
+createPatch(
+  { user: { name: 'Ada', active: false } },
+  { user: { name: 'Ada', active: true } },
+); // [{ op: 'replace', path: '/user/active', value: true }]
+```
+
 `applyPatch(document, patch)` applies an [RFC 6902 JSON Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6902)
 without mutating the source document. It supports `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy`, and
 `test`. Documents and operation members must be JSON values; operation members that RFC 6902 does
